introduction :
--------------
Hi, I’m Srinivas, an SAP CPI Consultant with a strong background in software development.
I started my career working with Java, Kotlin, and Groovy, which helped me develop strong
programming and scripting skills. This foundation supports my ability to design and develop
flexible, scalable integrations using SAP (CPI).

I specialize in end-to-end iFlow development, using key CPI components like Content Modifier,
Router, Splitter/Gather, Aggregator, and Join. I have hands-on experience with Groovy scripting,
graphical mappings, XSLT, JSON transformations, and node functions.

I’ve integrated systems such as S/4HANA, Concur, and SuccessFactors using a wide range of adapters
including HTTP, SOAP, OData, IDoc, SFTP, JMS, JDBC, Mail, and RFC. I’m well-versed in handling secure
communication using OAuth 2.0, Basic Authentication, and Client Certificates.

My iFlows often include patterns like routing, message splitting, content enrichment, and exception
handling, and I design them with modularity in mind using Local Integration Processes and Exception Subprocesses.

I’ve also worked with SAP Event Mesh for event-driven integrations and used SAP API Management for
designing and securing APIs. In hybrid scenarios, I’ve configured SAP Cloud Connector for secure
connectivity and used SAP Open Connectors to integrate external SaaS platforms through unified APIs.

In my day-to-day role, I focus on developing, deploying, and monitoring integration flows, managing
transports using SAP TMS, and troubleshooting via CPI Monitor, Trace, and Logs. I follow best practices
like reducing payload size using filters and select queries, optimizing message exchange patterns,
and implementing strategic logging without impacting performance.

I’m passionate about building clean, efficient, and robust integration solutions with a strong focus
on error handling, reusability, and performance optimization.

